cases.why:
This pins C1 and C5:
- 200 with the title escaped in <title>, <h1> and the iframe's title attribute;
- exactly one <iframe> whose sandbox token set is exactly {allow-popups, allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox}, with referrerpolicy=no-referrer and src=/raw/<slug>;
- Cache-Control: private, no-cache.

C6:
- exactly one Content-Security-Policy equal to a.rawCSP(), replacing siteCSP;
- nosniff, Referrer-Policy no-referrer, CORP same-origin, ETag of the sha256 and Cache-Control no-cache;
- the body equals the uploaded bytes and there is no Set-Cookie;
- HEAD has the same headers and an empty body;
- the conditional GET answers 304.

cases.shape:
each isolation layer alone, plus the run controls:
- the same bytes with no CSP, under the sandbox attribute parsed from the reader page (attribute alone);
- the same under sandbox=allow-scripts (positive control);
- /raw/<slug> framed from a foreign-port origin (blank)

cross_domain_transfer.pattern:
A negative result counts only when, in the same run, a positive control produced the signal and a blank produced none. The readout is a whole-well colour measurement with a dye chosen not to overlap the instrument's background, and the 'sample is present' signal does not depend on the chemistry under test.

Here:
- the report is a reagent, painted green by inline CSS (rendered and inert) and red by any script;
- the wells are Edge screenshots: the reader page over http and https, top-level /raw, attribute-only, a scripts-allowed positive control, and a frame-ancestors blank;
- the plate reader is image/png pixel counting;
- a run whose positive control is not red, or whose blank shows colour, is invalid and the test fails.

cross_domain_transfer.rationale:
The planned beacon test failed the way an assay fails when the buffer holds an inhibitor: img-src data: suppressed the only signal that showed the frame rendered, so silence meant nothing. Lab QC's answer is structural:
- separate the 'present' signal from the 'reaction' signal: green comes from style-src 'unsafe-inline', which rawCSP allows;
- read the whole well: no coordinates, so the spike's inline-style and box-model traps cannot bite;
- gate every run on controls.
The https well was added to the plate from the practice proposal.
